{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Moses assembled all the congregation of the children of Israel</b> — \"all the congregation of the children of Israel\" includes the men and the women, for all of them gave freewill offerings for the work of the Tabernacle. Now, after Moses had commanded Aaron and the leaders and all the children of Israel — the men — concerning everything that HaShem had spoken with him on Mount Sinai after the breaking of the tablets (Exodus 34:32), and had placed the veil over his face (ibid. v. 33), he again commanded and assembled all the congregation to him, men and women. And it is possible that this was on the day after his descent. And he said to all of them the matter of the Tabernacle concerning which he had been commanded initially, before the breaking of the tablets. For since HaShem had been reconciled to them and had given him the second tablets and made a new covenant with them — that HaShem would go in their midst — behold, they had returned to their former state and to the love of their betrothal, and it was known that His Shekhinah would be among them in the same manner concerning which He had commanded him at first, as He said (Exodus 25:8), \"And they shall make me a sanctuary and I will dwell among them.\" Therefore Moses now commanded them concerning everything he had been commanded initially:" "<b>These are the things which HaShem commanded to make them — six days shall work be done</b> — He said, <b>these are the things which HaShem commanded to make</b>, concerning the work of the Tabernacle and all its vessels and all its service, and he prefaced the Sabbath, saying: for six days these things shall be worked on, but not on the seventh day, which is holy to HaShem. From here we learn that the work of the Tabernacle does not override the Sabbath — and this is not derived from the midrash of \"אך\" ('however'), as I explained in the portion of Ki Tissa (Ramban on Exodus 31:13)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:21:52.272261894Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}